From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-ipq5018: keep the NSS core clock enabled

Keep the bootloader-enabled UBI0 core branch running until the NSS driver
claims it. Gating it in clk_disable_unused() and enabling it again at
module load can leave the Wi-Fi offload path unable to consume buffers.
A later enabled clock readback does not exclude this earlier transition.

Backport the pinned reference's single-clock fix to Linux 6.12. On WF810DF,
an unchanged internal-only RAM image with clk_ignore_unused continues
processing status messages and empty buffers after radio initialization,
unlike repeated boots without that argument. The global argument is only
a diagnostic: this patch preserves the UBI0 core branch alone. Dual-radio,
AP traffic and cold-power-cycle validation remain required.

Reference: kuncy7/openwrt-nss-edma 9caa35b4d718382ad882cb35c2372dbb569de901
Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq5018.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq5018.c
@@ -2881,7 +2881,7 @@ static struct clk_branch gcc_ubi0_core_clk = {
 				&ubi0_core_clk_src.clkr.hw,
 			},
 			.num_parents = 1,
-			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED,
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
 		},
 	},
